```

## Zero-second videos
#### Inspect videos that are "zero" seconds in duration
These "zero second" posts utilize the slideshow feature in TikTok. While they often contain meaningful on-screen text, it is not captured by the current coding process. The audio is most often trending music, which is not meaningful to the content analysis. The post description does contain meaningful information related to this study, and is captured by the coding process. Vidoes are ultimately not omitted in this round of cleaning, and are left to the discretion of manual content analysis. 
```{r, echo=FALSE, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE}
## How many videos are "zero" seconds
cat("How many videos are 'zero' seconds?")
sum(meta$duration_s == 0, na.rm = TRUE)
## Inspect a few of these videos by manually cross referencing with the URL
meta %>%
  filter(duration_s == 0) %>%
  select(tiktokurl, duration_s, item_id, on_screen_text_clean, desc_clean, transcript_clean) %>%
  head(10)
```

## English Language
#### Filtering posts by language
Retain posts that are indicated "en" and "un" under the "text_lang" column, to ensure English language posts in the data. "Unknown" language is often English language especially in this dataset: prescription names obfuscate language labelers.

```{r}
names(meta)
meta_success <- filter(meta,  transcriptionstatus == "success")
meta_en <- filter(meta, text_lang == "en" | text_lang == "un")
meta_success_en <- filter(meta_success, text_lang == "en" | text_lang == "un")
names(meta_success_en)
```


